iney\nCreek, Running Creek, North Garber Creek, Pine Creek, Coal Creek,\nKinney Creek, West Toll Gate Creek, Willow Creek, Plum Creek,\nAntelope Creek, Bayou Gulch, First Creek, Watson Park Creek, Dry\nGulch, Happy Canyon Creek, Lake Gulch, South Platte River and\nEast Toll Gate Creek. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1\ninch are expected over the area. This additional rain will result\nin minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSouthern Aurora, eastern Centennial, Castle Rock, Parker, Lone\nTree, Larkspur, Castle Pines, Franktown, Sedalia, The Pinery,\nPerry Park, Ponderosa Park, Devil's Head, Arapahoe Park,\nFoxfield, Castlewood Canyon and Shamballa.","ends":"2026-07-29T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.13e662d6e196dc40e2d5e38b16af1442896771da.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.13e662d6e196dc40e2d5e38b16af1442896771da.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-07-29T20:56:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 292056 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 256 PM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers and thunderstorms likely across the high terrain in the late morning, shifting to the plains by the afternoon. - Strong storms could produce localized flash flooding, particularly for the burn scar and areas along and east of the southern I-25 Corr","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-07-29T21:12:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Tonight and Thursday... Localized heavy rainfall may lead to flash flooding over the burn scars this afternoon and evening, as well as over areas that also received rainfall Tuesday afternoon. Shower and thunderstorm activity will diminish around 2100 MDT, although a few weak storms may linger until a bit later in the evening, particularly